# 01 - Network Setup


##Dilemma: We now have 2 working operating systems that sit on the virtualbox but have no way of communicating since they have no IP address and no network for that matter for them to share
##Objective: Ping each other's IP address to notify that the 2 OS are on the same network
Steps

1) Set both VMs to Internal Network name it "labnet" purpose: (so they can reach each other while staying isolated from the host network and internet)
2) Great we created a "fake" network; now we need to make fake IDs for our OS, in other words; IP addresses.
3) I did this manually by assigning them since there is no router and therefore no DHCP to assign them for me

On the Metasploitable terminal:
4) terminal> sudo ifconfig eth0 192.168.50.10

on the Kali terminal:
5) terminal> sudo ifconfig eth0 192.168.50.20

Now check the config to see if the address has been correctly manually given
6) terminal> ifconfig

** You noticed that Both devices are on the same subnet, 192.168.50.0/24 (subnet mask 255.255.255.0). This mask means the first three octets identify the network,
and the last octet identifies each device. Kali (192.168.50.20) and Metasploitable (192.168.50.10) share the same network portion and only differ in the last number.

7)Now vice versa we can ping each other's IP addresses on the other's OS terminal to see if there is connection and there will be packets that deliver successfully
